      "model": "gpt-6-astra",
      "question": "Our failure mode list for transformers looks thin to me. Pull the failure modes we currently have on file for a transformer, then suggest up to 4 more that an oil-immersed unit like Transformer 1 at site MAIN could realistically develop, such as corrosive sulfur deposition or bushing faults. For each suggested mode, tell me which of these channels would detect it: hydrogen, methane, ethane, ethylene, acetylene, co, co2, oxygen, nitrogen, dbds, dielectric_rigidity, interfacial_v, oti, oti_a, oti_t, ati, il1, il2, il3 or inut. Also check whether those channels actually have data between 2024-01-15T00:00:00.000000 and 2024-01-19T00:00:00.000000. Recommend adding only the modes that at least one channel with data can detect, and tell me which ones you left out and why. Don't recommend anything that duplicates an existing mode, even if the wording is different, and don't change the stored list yourself. If none of the suggestions survive, say that the current list stands.",
      "answer": "### Currently on file\nThe transformer catalog contains nine modes and is marked **non-exhaustive**:\n\n1. Partial Discharge in Oil\n2. Thermal Fault \u2014 Oil Overheating\n3. Thermal Fault \u2014 Core/Winding\n4. Low-Energy Arcing (Sparking)\n5. High-Energy Arcing\n6. Tap Changer Mechanical Wear\n7. Oil Contamination / Moisture Ingress\n8. Cellulose Insulation Ageing\n9. Oil Dielectric Degradation\n\n### Data availability\nFor **Transformer 1, MAIN**, all **20 channels you listed** have **four numeric readings each**, with no null readings reported, from January 15\u201318, 2024.\n\nThe query used **2024-01-15T00:00:00.000000 inclusive to 2024-01-19T00:00:00.000000 exclusive**.\n\n### Four candidates screened\n\n| Candidate | Relevant allowed channels and limitations | Recommendation |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Corrosive sulfur / copper-sulfide deposition** | `dbds` detects a sulfur-related precursor, **not deposited copper sulfide**. `dielectric_rigidity` and fault gases can indicate subsequent damage but cannot identify this mechanism. All have data. | **Leave out under your detection requirement:** precursor monitoring supports risk screening, not detection of deposition itself. |\n| **Bushing insulation failure** | `hydrogen`, `acetylene` could indicate discharge **if sampling the affected bushing oil**; main-tank measurements do not reliably monitor sealed bushings. `il1`, `il2`, `il3`, `inut` can show eventual electrical disturbance, not identify a bushing defect. All have data, but bushing-specific coverage is unverified. | **Leave out:** no demonstrated bushing-specific detection with these channels. |\n| **Oil oxidation / sludge formation** | `interfacial_v` can screen for oxidation products; `dielectric_rigidity` indicates associated loss of dielectric strength. Both have data. | **Leave out:** overlaps existing Oil Dielectric Degradation / Oil Contamination. |\n| **Cooling-system failure** | `oti`, supported by `ati` and `il1`\u2013`il3`, can reveal excessive temperature for ambient/load; `oti_a`, `oti_t` provide alarm/trip indications once their encoding is verified. All have data. | **Leave out:** these detect the already-listed Oil Overheating consequence, not uniquely a cooling-component failure. |\n\n**The current list stands under your detection and non-duplication rules.** Data availability alone does not establish diagnostic capability. No stored records were changed.",
      "score": {
